TOP PRIORITY B0 DOCUMENTATION SLICE FOR THE OWNERS NAMED VIDEO-RECALL TARGET.

Role: Sherlock is the canonical target pair for the external local video-recall vertical, while its current status is SelectedPendingDecision and NotAdmitted. It remains a coder-atlas diagnostic, not a vendored fixture, direct episode truth, calibrated validation corpus, or replacement for War of the Ghosts. Lawful F2 status requires the separate rights and human-source authority gates.

Exact repository paths:
1. docs/design/sherlock-local-pair-admission-court.md, new.
2. .gitignore, add a root-anchored /tmp/ rule only so the present media, annotation, participant artifacts, nested checkout, aliases, and future local manifests cannot enter ordinary Git status.

The court records only content-free identities and aggregate facts already measured: two media artifact digests and stream metadata; annotation artifact digest, row/schema counts, two-run discontinuity, missing TR coordinates, and 10.8 second unannotated tail; recall count and aggregate coverage; upstream release and conversion lineage status. Do not reproduce episode, annotation, participant, frame, word, filename, or participant-level digest content.

Required distinctions:
- selection, local byte presence, rights, participant authority, derivation receipt, semantic authority, and admissibility are independent axes;
- the owners instruction authorizes organization and planning only, not licence, consent, REB, redistribution, remote processing, or publication;
- source video, coder atlas, recall transcripts, scanner clocks, run-local seconds, stitched seconds, TR coordinates, media PTS, and future edition playback axis do not share a bare coordinate;
- XLSX to TSV and XLSX to CSV conversions remain unestablished until receipted;
- all 16 sub-N aliases are quarantined from canonical identity until one complete checked 17-entry mapping establishes source, omission, and pseudonym policy; no alias is deleted or trusted;
- participant bytes and raw hashes remain local-sensitive; use the project SensitiveDigest boundary for any future receipted identity rather than publishing reusable plaintext content hashes;
- TopicHmmEvent30 is recall-tuned diagnostic lineage and never independent gold;
- first result may claim agreement with the coder atlas only, under a SourceFrozen or properly cross-fitted lineage and a predeclared question.

This slice does not amend ADR 0007, close B0/P1, create SourceBundle or PresentationAxis APIs, implement a verifier/adapter, process participant prose, accept terms, or admit any data.

Author gate: git diff --check; exact two-path diff; git ls-files under tmp is empty; git check-ignore proves representative media, annotation, recall, nested-checkout, and future-manifest paths are ignored; no participant filename patterns or content excerpts appear in the new doc; source-line checklist against ADR 0007, the Sherlock audit, plan sections 8 through 12, Constitution IX, codec README plain-StorySource warning, and SensitiveDigest docs. Independent review by codex-storymodel4s-recall-collab and codex-storymodel4s-collab after immutable SHA.
